email in one respect — but Raj said \"We agreed to start the rebrand on October 5\", and this is the calendar''s version. Note Raj himself isn''t an attendee of the kickoff; Tomás and Kenji are. That answers half of Raj''s question — Tomás was on the kickoff invite.\n3. The 8 Oct 15:00 slot: email invited to \"Rebrand review\" but the Work calendar entry at exactly that time is titled **\"Design review\"** (15:00–16:00, Studio 2, no attendees). Worth flagging as a likely match, not certain.\n4. **Tokyo trip** — all-day, Mon 9 Nov – Sun 15 Nov 2026, Personal calendar. Ties the flight to the trip; no attendees.\n\nNothing rebrand-specific after 9 Oct. Nothing upcoming.\n\nAlso note: the entire window query returned 250 results (capped), mostly Bulk/Edge noise — those are unrelated calendars. I should say the calendars include a \"Bulk\" and \"Edge cases\" calendar full of synthetic-looking entries; not needed.\n\nShould I mention caveat that a search by title only catches title matches, and \"Design review\" is a candidate? Yes.\n\nFormat nicely.\n\nAlso mention: no rebrand event is in the future; the last is 9 Oct. Kickoff Oct 5 conflicts with \"Implantação da República (holiday)\" all-day on Personal — irrelevant maybe. Actually interesting: Oct 5 is a Portuguese holiday and the kickoff was on that date. Not necessary.\n\nLet me write it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now report. Calendars visible: one account, ana@demo.trymetis.email, four calendars: Bulk, Edge cases, Personal, Work.\n\nRebrand-related events (all in the **Work** calendar except Tokyo trip on Personal):\n\n1. **Aozora logo review (internal)** — Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 2, Work calendar. Attendees: ana, tomas.\n2. **Aozora rebrand kickoff** — Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, https://linkroom.app/r/aozora-kickoff, Work calendar. Attendees: ana, tomas, kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp. This matches Raj''s email in one respect — but Raj said \"We agreed to start the rebrand on October 5\", and this is the calendar''s version. Note Raj himself isn''t an attendee of the kickoff; Tomás and Kenji are. That answers half of Raj''s question — Tomás was on the kickoff invite.\n3. The 8 Oct 15:00 slot: email invited to \"Rebrand review\" but the Work calendar entry at exactly that time is titled **\"Design review\"** (15:00–16:00, Studio 2, no attendees). Worth flagging as a likely match, not certain.\n4. **Tokyo trip** — all-day, Mon 9 Nov – Sun 15 Nov 2026, Personal calendar. Ties the flight to the trip; no attendees.\n\nNothing rebrand-specific after 9 Oct. Nothing upcoming.\n\nAlso note: the entire window query returned 250 results (capped), mostly Bulk/Edge noise — those are unrelated calendars. I should say the calendars include a \"Bulk\" and \"Edge cases\" calendar full of synthetic-looking entries; not needed.\n\nShould I mention caveat that a search by title only catches title matches, and \"Design review\" is a candidate? Yes.\n\nFormat nicely.\n\nAlso mention: no rebrand event is in the future; the last is 9 Oct. Kickoff Oct 5 conflicts with \"Implantação da República (holiday)\" all-day on Personal — irrelevant maybe. Actually interesting: Oct 5 is a Portuguese holiday and the kickoff was on that date. Not necessary.\n\nLet me write it."}],"createdAt":1794305923262},{"type":"text","text":"**Yes — three events, all past.** Everything the workspace can see sits on one account, **ana@demo.trymetis.email**, which exposes four calendars (Work, Personal, Bulk, Edge cases).\n\n## Rebrand events found\n- **Aozora logo review (internal)** — **Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC**, Studio 2 — *Work* calendar. Attendees: ana@demo.trymetis.email, tomas@demo.trymetis.email. This is the meeting the \"Updated invitation\" email was about.\n- **Aozora rebrand kickoff** — **Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC**, https://linkroom.app/r/aozora-kickoff — *Work* calendar. Attendees: ana@demo.trymetis.email, tomas@demo.trymetis.email, **kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp**.\n- **Tokyo trip** — all-day, **Mon 9 Nov – Sun 15 Nov 2026** — *Personal* calendar. No attendees; this is the trip the changed Frankfurt–Haneda flight belongs to.\n\n## Two things worth noting\n**The kickoff answers half of Raj''s email.** Tomás *was* on the 5 Oct kickoff invitation, which is the \"can Tomás join the first review?\" question — though the calendar''s kickoff includes Tomás and Kenji, not Raj. Raj''s email and this event agree the start date was 5 Oct.\n\n**The 8 Oct \"Rebrand review\" doesn''t exist under that name.** Raj''s invitation was for Thu 8 Oct, 15:00–15:45 UTC. At exactly that slot the *Work* calendar holds **\"Design review\"** — 15:00–16:00, Studio 2, no attendees listed. That is very likely the same meeting under a different title, but I can''t confirm it from the data, so treat it as a probable match rather than a fact.\n\nNothing rebrand-related is scheduled after 9 Oct, and nothing is coming up — the sequence ran 1 Oct → 5 Oct → 8/9 Oct and then stopped. Given the moodboard was due 25 Sep and Raj''s kickoff was 21 Sep, the thread appears to have gone quiet right after the review rather than being carried forward.\n\nWant me to correct the 8 Oct entry to \"Rebrand review\", or add a follow-up event so the rebrand doesn''t stay stalled?","createdAt":1794305923262}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Yes — three events, all past.** Everything the workspace can see sits on one account, **ana@demo.trymetis.email**, which exposes four calendars (Work, Personal, Bulk, Edge cases).\n\n## Rebrand events found\n- **Aozora logo review (internal)** — **Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC**, Studio 2 — *Work* calendar. Attendees: ana@demo.trymetis.email, tomas@demo.trymetis.email. This is the meeting the \"Updated invitation\" email was about.\n- **Aozora rebrand kickoff** — **Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC**, https://linkroom.app/r/aozora-kickoff — *Work* calendar. Attendees: ana@demo.trymetis.email, tomas@demo.trymetis.email, **kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp**.\n- **Tokyo trip** — all-day, **Mon 9 Nov – Sun 15 Nov 2026** — *Personal* calendar. No attendees; this is the trip the changed Frankfurt–Haneda flight belongs to.\n\n## Two things worth noting\n**The kickoff answers half of Raj''s email.** Tomás *was* on the 5 Oct kickoff invitation, which is the \"can Tomás join the first review?\" question — though the calendar''s kickoff includes Tomás and Kenji, not Raj. Raj''s email and this event agree the start date was 5 Oct.\n\n**The 8 Oct \"Rebrand review\" doesn''t exist under that name.** Raj''s invitation was for Thu 8 Oct, 15:00–15:45 UTC. At exactly that slot the *Work* calendar holds **\"Design review\"** — 15:00–16:00, Studio 2, no attendees listed. That is very likely the same meeting under a different title, but I can''t confirm it from the data, so treat it as a probable match rather than a fact.\n\nNothing rebrand-related is scheduled after 9 Oct, and nothing is coming up — the sequence ran 1 Oct → 5 Oct → 8/9 Oct and then stopped. Given the moodboard was due 25 Sep and Raj''s kickoff was 21 Sep, the thread appears to have gone quiet right after the review rather than being carried forward.\n\nWant me to correct the 8 Oct entry to \"Rebrand review\", or add a follow-up event so the rebrand doesn''t stay stalled?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T10:18:15.569Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
