,"end":"2026-10-08T13:30:00.000Z","allDay":false,"location":"https://linkroom.app/r/print-vendor","attendees":["priya@demo.trymetis.email"]},{"eventId":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/work/design-review.ics","calendarAccountId":"ef21568e-53a9-597d-bc5c-451f8029a9de","accountEmail":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","calendarId":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/work/","calendarName":"Work","title":"Design review","start":"2026-10-08T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T16:00:00.000Z","allDay":false,"location":"Studio 2","attendees":[]}]},"toolCallId":"call_4ca13fa4e4764de09903c991","toolName":"listEvents","args":{"max":250,"timeMax":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","timeMin":"2026-10-08T00:00:00Z"}},"updatedAt":1794305982735},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1794305982739,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Thursday 8 Oct 2026, all calendars (one account, four calendars).\n\nTimeline:\n- All-day: \"Ten year all-day event\" (Edge cases) — spans 2026-01-01 to 2036-01-01, so technically present every day. Mention as noise.\n- 09:00–09:15 Daily standup (Work), linkroom standup\n- 09:00–09:15 Daily forever (Edge cases, recurring) — clutter\n- 10:00–13:00 Workshop: packaging prototypes, Studio 2 (Work), ana + raj + priya\n- 13:00–13:30 Print vendor call (Pune), linkroom (Work), ana + priya\n- 15:00–16:00 Design review (= the rebrand review), Studio 2, Work, no attendees listed\n\nSo the review is boxed: a 3-hour packaging workshop right before, a print vendor call next, and the review itself. Nothing in Personal calendar. No conflicts with the review.\n\nNote: the packaging workshop attendees include Raj and Priya — and the brief''s deliverables include packaging for mugs/plates/gift box, so the workshop is directly connected to rebrand work. Worth noting as rebrand-adjacent.\n\nReport in a clean timeline. Note the \"Design review\" listing as the review (per prior conclusion).\n\nAlso say nothing on the Personal calendar that day, and the two all-day/recurring entries are clutter.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Thursday 8 Oct 2026, all calendars (one account, four calendars).\n\nTimeline:\n- All-day: \"Ten year all-day event\" (Edge cases) — spans 2026-01-01 to 2036-01-01, so technically present every day. Mention as noise.\n- 09:00–09:15 Daily standup (Work), linkroom standup\n- 09:00–09:15 Daily forever (Edge cases, recurring) — clutter\n- 10:00–13:00 Workshop: packaging prototypes, Studio 2 (Work), ana + raj + priya\n- 13:00–13:30 Print vendor call (Pune), linkroom (Work), ana + priya\n- 15:00–16:00 Design review (= the rebrand review), Studio 2, Work, no attendees listed\n\nSo the review is boxed: a 3-hour packaging workshop right before, a print vendor call next, and the review itself. Nothing in Personal calendar. No conflicts with the review.\n\nNote: the packaging workshop attendees include Raj and Priya — and the brief''s deliverables include packaging for mugs/plates/gift box, so the workshop is directly connected to rebrand work. Worth noting as rebrand-adjacent.\n\nReport in a clean timeline. Note the \"Design review\" listing as the review (per prior conclusion).\n\nAlso say nothing on the Personal calendar that day, and the two all-day/recurring entries are clutter."}],"createdAt":1794305995330},{"type":"text","text":"**Thursday 8 Oct 2026** — six entries, all on the one account (ana@demo.trymetis.email). Three of them are real work; the rest is clutter.\n\n| Time (UTC) | Event | Calendar | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| all day | Ten year all-day event | Edge cases | noise — spans 2026 → 2036, so it shows on every day |\n| 09:00–09:15 | Daily standup | Work | linkroom.app/r/standup |\n| 09:00–09:15 | Daily forever | Edge cases | noise — daily recurring clutter |\n| 10:00–13:00 | **Workshop: packaging prototypes** | Work | Studio 2 — ana, raj, priya |\n| 13:00–13:30 | **Print vendor call (Pune)** | Work | linkroom.app/r/print-vendor — ana, priya |\n| 15:00–16:00 | **Design review** ← *the rebrand review* | Work | Studio 2 — no attendees listed |\n\n**The day is built around the project.** The review at 15:00 sits at the end of a run that is entirely Aozora work: a three-hour packaging-prototype session in the morning — and packaging for the mugs, plates and gift box is one of the brief''s three deliverables — then the print vendor call, then the review itself. Nothing conflicts with it and nothing on the Personal calendar that day.\n\nWorth flagging: **the morning workshop had Raj and Priya on it, but the 15:00 review has no attendees at all** — consistent with it being the entry Raj''s invitation never got attached to. That''s another sign the calendar record for this project was never properly kept up.","createdAt":1794305995330}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Thursday 8 Oct 2026** — six entries, all on the one account (ana@demo.trymetis.email). Three of them are real work; the rest is clutter.\n\n| Time (UTC) | Event | Calendar | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| all day | Ten year all-day event | Edge cases | noise — spans 2026 → 2036, so it shows on every day |\n| 09:00–09:15 | Daily standup | Work | linkroom.app/r/standup |\n| 09:00–09:15 | Daily forever | Edge cases | noise — daily recurring clutter |\n| 10:00–13:00 | **Workshop: packaging prototypes** | Work | Studio 2 — ana, raj, priya |\n| 13:00–13:30 | **Print vendor call (Pune)** | Work | linkroom.app/r/print-vendor — ana, priya |\n| 15:00–16:00 | **Design review** ← *the rebrand review* | Work | Studio 2 — no attendees listed |\n\n**The day is built around the project.** The review at 15:00 sits at the end of a run that is entirely Aozora work: a three-hour packaging-prototype session in the morning — and packaging for the mugs, plates and gift box is one of the brief''s three deliverables — then the print vendor call, then the review itself. Nothing conflicts with it and nothing on the Personal calendar that day.\n\nWorth flagging: **the morning workshop had Raj and Priya on it, but the 15:00 review has no attendees at all** — consistent with it being the entry Raj''s invitation never got attached to. That''s another sign the calendar record for this project was never properly kept up."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T10:19:42.679Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
