e flag. Everything else (A-38 delivered 4 Aug, A-31 delivered 24 Apr) is old and complete.\n\nNote \"recently\" — 23 Sep is 7 weeks ago; it''s the most recent shipment. And it appears stalled/undelivered.\n\nAlso the Kestrel Supply Co. emails: \"This week at the shop\" and \"15% off\" are marketing, not orders. No order there.\n\nI should be measured: I can''t see the actual parcel status — the mailbox just shows no further Swiftpost updates. Suggest checking/track, or the \"Track your package\" link in the email.\n\nOffer: draft a chase to Brightloom? Or find the tracking link. Keep the offer short.\n\nReport the mailbox: ana@demo.trymetis.email."}],"createdAt":1794306036404},{"type":"text","text":"**Yes — one, and it''s worth chasing.** In **ana@demo.trymetis.email** (your only connected mailbox):\n\n## Brightloom order A-42 — the walnut desk lamp\n- **Placed** Fri 18 Sep 2026 (\"Thanks for your order A-42\")\n- **Shipped** Wed 23 Sep 2026 — *\"your order A-42 is on its way. Walnut desk lamp, shipped with Swiftpost.* **Expected by September 30.**\"\n- **Since then: nothing.** No Swiftpost \"on its way\", no \"out for delivery\", no \"delivered\".\n\nThat silence is the story. **Expected 30 Sep; today is 10 Nov — six weeks past its own delivery estimate, seven weeks since it shipped.** Your other Brightloom orders each produced a full Swiftpost sequence — A-38 shipped 1 Aug, delivered 4 Aug; A-31 shipped 15 Apr, delayed 20 Apr, delivered 24 Apr — so the carrier normally does keep you posted. A-42 just stops dead after the shop''s own notice.\n\nNothing else is live. The other order mail is historical and closed: A-38 (Aug), A-31 (Apr), A-23 (Jun 2025), A-17 (Feb 2025). The Kestrel Supply Co. messages are newsletters, not orders.\n\nThe 23 Sep email ends with a \"Track your package\" link — that''s the fastest way to see whether Swiftpost ever scanned it. Want me to draft a chase to Brightloom quoting A-42 and the 30 Sep estimate?","createdAt":1794306036404}],"metad