nbox\"\n\nBoth in parallel.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user asks about tracking for A-42. I should read the full email bodies of the A-42 emails (the shipped one had \"Track your package\" as a link, but maybe the full body has tracking number — the body I got was short). Let me also check the Swiftpost emails to see if any corresponds to A-42 — e.g., the Swiftpost \"Your parcel from Brightloom is on its way\" Aug 1 body may reference a tracking number and order. Also the shipped email might have attachment? Unlikely.\n\nAlso check whether there''s a Swiftpost email that mentions A-42 but didn''t match \"Brightloom\"/\"shipped\"/\"delivery\" searches — e.g., a \"delayed\" or \"delivered\" message. Search \"Swiftpost\" to get all Swiftpost messages.\n\nLet me do: searchMail \"Swiftpost\", and getEmail for the two Swiftpost \"on its way\" emails (Aug 1 and Apr 15) plus maybe delivered ones to compare tracking numbers. Actually the key: read the A-42 shipped email fully — I already have the body; it says \"Track your package\" as a link text, no tracking number visible in plain text. Maybe listAttachments? Let me search for a tool to see links? There''s no such tool probably.\n\nBest: search \"Swiftpost\" to enumerate all carrier messages, and read the ones from around late Sep / early Oct. If none exist in Sep/Oct, then the tracking situation = never handed to carrier / no carrier events.\n\nLet me also list the whole inbox? The aggregateInbox could reveal the recent window. But the mailbox''s inbox recent items — I haven''t seen the full inbox list. Actually I don''t have a list-by-folder tool loaded (\"one folder of one mailbox\"). Let me search for that too: \"list folder mailbox inbox\".\n\nPlan this turn: \n1. searchMail \"Swiftpost\"\n2. search_tools \"list emails in a folder inbox\"\n\nBoth in parallel."}],"createdAt":1794306042930},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":12,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea