 but that''s July 28, before A-42 (Sep 18). So that''s likely for A-38 or something else. Hmm, A-38 ordered Jul 30... so Jul 28 is before A-38''s order too. So that spam \"could not deliver\" is July 28 — unassociated with A-42. Careful: don''t attribute it to A-42. And the domain \"swiftpost-redelivery.co\" is suspicious (a phishing lookalike vs swiftpost.com). Actually the real Swiftpost uses @swiftpost.com. So that spam email is probably a phishing lure. Also note it''s a \"could not deliver your parcel\" phish, dated Jul 28.\n\nWait — but the user asks about the tracking situation for A-42. Key facts:\n- A-42 shipped 23 Sep via Swiftpost per Brightloom''s notice, expected by 30 Sep.\n- The email''s only tracking affordance is a \"Track your package\" link (no tracking number in the plain text).\n- No Swiftpost carrier email exists for A-42 at all — none in inbox, archive, spam (the only spam carrier message is the Jul 28 delivery-failure phish, which predates the order), or trash.\n- For comparison, A-38 got parcel **SP4471920368PT** — a real tracking number format. A-42 never got one from the carrier.\n\nSo the tracking situation: A-42 has no carrier-issued tracking number anywhere; the Brightloom email contains a \"Track your package\" link but no number; there is no Swiftpost scan history for A-42. Either Brightloom''s \"shipped\" notice was generated without an actual handover, or the carrier never scanned/sent.\n\nAlso, the archive had \"आपका पार्सल डिलीवरी के लिए निकल चुका है\" (Oct 11 2025) — Hindi for \"your parcel is out for delivery\" — older, for a prior parcel.\n\nI should also mention the spam message explicitly because the user might think it relates: it''s dated 28 Jul, before A-42 existed, comes from a lookalike domain (swiftpost-redelivery.co, not swiftpost.com), and is unread — likely phishing. Important: do NOT get the user to click. Actually, careful with attributing phishing definitively, but I can note the mismatch: real Swiftpost mails come from swiftpost.com.\n\nShould I read that spam email body to check? It could reference a parcel number. Worth reading to be accurate — it might mention a parcel ID and whether it''s A-42. Let me read it. Also maybe check if there''s a tracking number pattern. I''ll read it.\n\nAlso check inbox page 2? The inbox list of 50 ended at Aug 9 with nextPageToken. The recent items are covered; the A-42-relevant window (23 Sep onward) is at the top. Before 23 Sep is covered. So fine. But there could be a Swiftpost message in the Sep 23–Nov 10 window that''s not in the top-50? No — the top 50 spans Sep 26 back to Aug 9; the newest inbox item is 26 Sep. So the inbox has NOTHING after 26 Sep 2026 at all! Wait, the first item is Sep 26 \"This week at the shop\", then Sep 25 bank... so the newest email in the inbox is 26 Sep. That confirms silence since 26 Sep.\n\nHmm, but the mailbox overall newest: searchMail results showed newest was Sep 26 too. So the whole mailbox''s newest mail is 26 Sep — nothing since. So no delivery mail for A-42 could have arrived after 26 Sep anyway (nothing arrived at all). Interesting: the mailbox has received nothing since Sep 26 — 6+ weeks. That''s a notable observation. Actually that''s suspicious in itself; but combined: whatever happened with A-42, no mail arrived since Sep 26 to report it.\n\nLet me read the spam message and maybe the \"out for delivery\" Aug 4 one for A-38 to confirm the tracking format. Also read the delivered emails? I have enough: A-38''s tracking number SP4471920368PT.\n\nLet me read the spam one.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Key finding! In the **Spam** folder there''s:\n\n\"We could not deliver your parcel\" from **Swiftpost Delivery** <427o1vxtefbgvd6b@swiftpost-redelivery.co>, Tue Jul 28 2026 — but that''s July 28, before A-42 (Sep 18). So that''s likely for A-38 or something else. Hmm, A-38 ordered Jul 30... so Jul 28 is before A-38''s order too. So that spam \"could not deliver\" is July 28 — unassociated with A-42. Careful: don''t attribute it to A-42. And the domain \"swiftpost-redelivery.co\" is suspicious (a phishing lookalike vs swiftpost.com). Actually the real Swiftpost uses @swiftpost.com. So that spam email is probably a phishing lure. Also note it''s a \"could not deliver your parcel\" phish, dated Jul 28.\n\nWait — but the user asks about the tracking situation for A-42. Key facts:\n- A-42 shipped 23 Sep via Swiftpost per Brightloom''s notice, expected by 30 Sep.\n- The email''s only tracking affordance is a \"Track your package\" link (no tracking number in the plain text).\n- No Swiftpost carrier email exists for A-42 at all — none in inbox, archive, spam (the only spam carrier message is the Jul 28 delivery-failure phish, which predates the order), or trash.\n- For comparison, A-38 got parcel **SP4471920368PT** — a real tracking number format. A-42 never got one from the carrier.\n\nSo the tracking situation: A-42 has no carrier-issued tracking number anywhere; the Brightloom email contains a \"Track your package\" link but no number; there is no Swiftpost scan history for A-42. Either Brightloom''s \"shipped\" notice was generated without an actual handover, or the carrier never scanned/sent.\n\nAlso, the archive had \"आपका पार्सल डिलीवरी के लिए निकल चुका है\" (Oct 11 2025) — Hindi for \"your parcel is out for delivery\" — older, for a prior parcel.\n\nI should also mention the spam message explicitly because the user might think it relates: it''s dated 28 Jul, before A-42 existed, comes from a lookalike domain (swiftpost-redelivery.co, not swiftpost.com), and is unread — likely phishing. Important: do NOT get the user to click. Actually, careful with attributing phishing definitively, but I can note the mismatch: real Swiftpost mails come from swiftpost.com.\n\nShould I read that spam email body to check? It could reference a parcel number. Worth reading to be accurate — it might mention a parcel ID and whether it''s A-42. Let me read it. Also maybe check if there''s a tracking number pattern. I''ll read it.\n\nAlso check inbox page 2? The inbox list of 50 ended at Aug 9 with nextPageToken. The recent items are covered; the A-42-relevant window (23 Sep onward) is at the top. Before 23 Sep is covered. So fine. But there could be a Swiftpost message in the Sep 23–Nov 10 window that''s not in the top-50? No — the top 50 spans Sep 26 back to Aug 9; the newest inbox item is 26 Sep. So the inbox has NOTHING after 26 Sep 2026 at all! Wait, the first item is Sep 26 \"This week at the shop\", then Sep 25 bank... so the newest email in the inbox is 26 Sep. That confirms silence since 26 Sep.\n\nHmm, but the mailbox overall newest: searchMail results showed newest was Sep 26 too. So the whole mailbox''s newest mail is 26 Sep — nothing since. So no delivery mail for A-42 could have arrived after 26 Sep anyway (nothing arrived at all). Interesting: the mailbox has received nothing since Sep 26 — 6+ weeks. That''s a notable observation. Actually that''s suspicious in itself; but combined: whatever happened with A-42, no mail arrived since Sep 26 to report it.\n\nLet me read the spam message and maybe the \"out for delivery\" Aug 4 one for A-38 to confirm the tracking format. Also read the delivered emails? I have enough: A-38''s tracking number SP4471920368PT.\n\nLet me read the spam one."}],"createdAt":1794306064305},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"WyJKdW5rIiwiMTAwMCIsOF0","from":"Swiftpost Delivery","to":["ana@demo.trymetis.email"],"subject":"We could not deliver your parcel","date":"Tue Jul 28 2026 11:30:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Your parcel is waiting at our depot. Pay the EUR 1.99 redelivery fee to schedule a new date. Pay and reschedule"},"toolCallId":"call_bb6d790a1a2f447dafbcb3e4","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"id":"WyJKdW5rIiwiMTAwMCIsOF0","mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134"}},"updatedAt":1794306064445},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM2MF0","from":"Swiftpost","to":["ana@demo.trymetis.email"],"subject":"Your Swiftpost parcel was delivered","date":"Tue Aug 04 2026 11:20:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Parcel SP4471920402PT for Brightloom order A-38: delivered . Delivered to your mailbox at 11:16. Track your parcel"},"toolCallId":"call_575dc353718b495994978d31","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM2MF0","mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134"}},"updatedAt":1794306064451},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1794306064521,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Confirmed:\n- A-38: parcel SP4471920368PT (shipped 1 Aug) → SP4471920402PT? Hmm, two different numbers: \"on its way\" says SP4471920368PT for A-38, and delivered says SP4471920402PT for A-38. Slightly odd (two parcel IDs), but fine — that''s a data quirk. Actually a bit inconsistent, maybe one per leg. I''ll mention A-38 had a parcel number SP4471920… starting with 4471920.\n\n- A-42: no parcel number at all anywhere. Brightloom''s shipped mail contains only \"Track your package\" link text.\n\n- Spam: \"Swiftpost Delivery\" from swiftpost-redelivery.co, Jul 28, asking for EUR 1.99 redelivery fee — classic fee-phishing, and it predates A-42 by seven weeks. Real Swiftpost mail comes from @swiftpost.com and never asks for a fee. Verdict: not A-42, and don''t pay it.\n\nLet me also double-check: is there any other mailbox? Only one mailbox (searchMail error listed just one). So we''re complete.\n\nAlso worth noting: mailbox has received nothing since 26 Sep 2026 — no mail at all in 6 weeks, so even if Swiftpost tried to notify, nothing''s landed.\n\nHmm, careful — \"nothing since 26 Sep\" is based on the inbox top-50 plus searches. The search results'' newest across all folders was Sep 26. I''ll state it as: the newest message anywhere in the mailbox is 26 Sep.\n\nNow compose the answer: the tracking situation.\n\nStructure:\n- Bottom line: A-42 has no tracking number and no carrier scan history. Only one thing came from the carrier chain, and it''s not from the real carrier.\n- The evidence chain table:\n  - 18 Sep: order confirmed, EUR 129, free shipping, no tracking\n  - 23 Sep: \"shipped\" — only \"Track your package\" link, no number; expected 30 Sep\n  - 1 Aug comparison: real Swiftpost gives parcel SP4471920368PT\n  - between 23 Sep and 10 Nov: zero messages from Swiftpost about A-42; in fact newest message anywhere in the mailbox = 26 Sep\n- The one carrier-shaped email is a phishing lure in Spam: 28 Jul, swiftpost-redelivery.co, EUR 1.99 redelivery fee — predates the order by 7 weeks, wrong domain, asks for payment. Don''t pay; it''s unread. (offer to delete/keep)\n- Verdict: either Brightloom''s \"shipped\" was generated before an actual handover, or the parcel number never reached you. Either way you can''t self-serve tracking; the only route is the email''s \"Track your package\" link or asking Brightloom for the number.\n\nOffer: draft chase to Brightloom asking for A-42''s Swiftpost number and status; and optionally delete the spam.\n\nKeep tight and scannable. Name the mailbox.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed:\n- A-38: parcel SP4471920368PT (shipped 1 Aug) → SP4471920402PT? Hmm, two different numbers: \"on its way\" says SP4471920368PT for A-38, and delivered says SP4471920402PT for A-38. Slightly odd (two parcel IDs), but fine — that''s a data quirk. Actually a bit inconsistent, maybe one per leg. I''ll mention A-38 had a parcel number SP4471920… starting with 4471920.\n\n- A-42: no parcel number at all anywhere. Brightloom''s shipped mail contains only \"Track your package\" link text.\n\n- Spam: \"Swiftpost Delivery\" from swiftpost-redelivery.co, Jul 28, asking for EUR 1.99 redelivery fee — classic fee-phishing, and it predates A-42 by seven weeks. Real Swiftpost mail comes from @swiftpost.com and never asks for a fee. Verdict: not A-42, and don''t pay it.\n\nLet me also double-check: is there any other mailbox? Only one mailbox (searchMail error listed just one). So we''re complete.\n\nAlso worth noting: mailbox has received nothing since 26 Sep 2026 — no mail at all in 6 weeks, so even if Swiftpost tried to notify, nothing''s landed.\n\nHmm, careful — \"nothing since 26 Sep\" is based on the inbox top-50 plus searches. The search results'' newest across all folders was Sep 26. I''ll state it as: the newest message anywhere in the mailbox is 26 Sep.\n\nNow compose the answer: the tracking situation.\n\nStructure:\n- Bottom line: A-42 has no tracking number and no carrier scan history. Only one thing came from the carrier chain, and it''s not from the real carrier.\n- The evidence chain table:\n  - 18 Sep: order confirmed, EUR 129, free shipping, no tracking\n  - 23 Sep: \"shipped\" — only \"Track your package\" link, no number; expected 30 Sep\n  - 1 Aug comparison: real Swiftpost gives parcel SP4471920368PT\n  - between 23 Sep and 10 Nov: zero messages from Swiftpost about A-42; in fact newest message anywhere in the mailbox = 26 Sep\n- The one carrier-shaped email is a phishing lure in Spam: 28 Jul, swiftpost-redelivery.co, EUR 1.99 redelivery fee — predates the order by 7 weeks, wrong domain, asks for payment. Don''t pay; it''s unread. (offer to delete/keep)\n- Verdict: either Brightloom''s \"shipped\" was generated before an actual handover, or the parcel number never reached you. Either way you can''t self-serve tracking; the only route is the email''s \"Track your package\" link or asking Brightloom for the number.\n\nOffer: draft chase to Brightloom asking for A-42''s Swiftpost number and status; and optionally delete the spam.\n\nKeep tight and scannable. Name the mailbox."}],"createdAt":1794306077483},{"type":"text","text":"**Bottom line: A-42 has no tracking number, and no carrier scan history at all.** Not missing from your view — never generated as far as ana@demo.trymetis.email can show.\n\n## The chain for A-42\n| When | From | What it gives you |\n|---|---|---|\n| 18 Sep, 19:02 | Brightloom — *Thanks for your order A-42* | confirmed, Walnut desk lamp EUR 129.00, free shipping — no number |\n| 23 Sep, 10:00 | Brightloom — *Your order A-42 has shipped* | \"shipped with Swiftpost\", expected by **30 Sep** — and only a **\"Track your package\"** link, **no parcel number in the text** |\n| 23 Sep → 10 Nov | — | **nothing.** Not one Swiftpost message mentioning A-42, in any folder |\n\nCompare a working order: **A-38** produced a real Swiftpost parcel number — *SP4471920368PT* on 1 Aug, then *SP4471920402PT* delivered 4 Aug — as did A-31 in April. A-42 produced none of that. So there is no number for you to paste into a tracker; the only thing available is the link inside Brightloom''s own email.\n\nWider point: **the newest message anywhere in your mailbox is 26 Sep 2026.** Nothing has arrived in seven weeks, so even a carrier notification sent after that date would not be here.\n\n## One thing to be aware of\nThere is exactly one other parcel-shaped email, sitting **unread in Spam**:\n\n> **Swiftpost Delivery** — *We could not deliver your parcel* — 28 Jul 2026, 11:30 — \"Your parcel is waiting at our depot. Pay the EUR 1.99 redelivery fee to schedule a new date.\"\n\n**This is not A-42.** It predates the order by seven weeks, it comes from `swiftpost-redelivery.co` while the real carrier writes from `swiftpost.com`, and real Swiftpost notifications never ask for a fee to redeliver. It''s a phishing lure, and it has been sitting there for over three months. Don''t pay it.\n\n## What that leaves you\nA-42''s tracking cannot be self-served. Either Brightloom''s shipping notice fired without a real handover to Swiftpost, or the parcel number never made it into the mail. Either way the fix is the same: **ask Brightloom for A-42''s Swiftpost tracking number and current status**, quoting the 30 Sep estimate — now six weeks overdue.\n\nWant me to draft that chase to Brightloom, and clear the phishing message out of Spam while I''m at it?","createdAt":1794306077483}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Bottom line: A-42 has no tracking number, and no carrier scan history at all.** Not missing from your view — never generated as far as ana@demo.trymetis.email can show.\n\n## The chain for A-42\n| When | From | What it gives you |\n|---|---|---|\n| 18 Sep, 19:02 | Brightloom — *Thanks for your order A-42* | confirmed, Walnut desk lamp EUR 129.00, free shipping — no number |\n| 23 Sep, 10:00 | Brightloom — *Your order A-42 has shipped* | \"shipped with Swiftpost\", expected by **30 Sep** — and only a **\"Track your package\"** link, **no parcel number in the text** |\n| 23 Sep → 10 Nov | — | **nothing.** Not one Swiftpost message mentioning A-42, in any folder |\n\nCompare a working order: **A-38** produced a real Swiftpost parcel number — *SP4471920368PT* on 1 Aug, then *SP4471920402PT* delivered 4 Aug — as did A-31 in April. A-42 produced none of that. So there is no number for you to paste into a tracker; the only thing available is the link inside Brightloom''s own email.\n\nWider point: **the newest message anywhere in your mailbox is 26 Sep 2026.** Nothing has arrived in seven weeks, so even a carrier notification sent after that date would not be here.\n\n## One thing to be aware of\nThere is exactly one other parcel-shaped email, sitting **unread in Spam**:\n\n> **Swiftpost Delivery** — *We could not deliver your parcel* — 28 Jul 2026, 11:30 — \"Your parcel is waiting at our depot. Pay the EUR 1.99 redelivery fee to schedule a new date.\"\n\n**This is not A-42.** It predates the order by seven weeks, it comes from `swiftpost-redelivery.co` while the real carrier writes from `swiftpost.com`, and real Swiftpost notifications never ask for a fee to redeliver. It''s a phishing lure, and it has been sitting there for over three months. Don''t pay it.\n\n## What that leaves you\nA-42''s tracking cannot be self-served. Either Brightloom''s shipping notice fired without a real handover to Swiftpost, or the parcel number never made it into the mail. Either way the fix is the same: **ask Brightloom for A-42''s Swiftpost tracking number and current status**, quoting the 30 Sep estimate — now six weeks overdue.\n\nWant me to draft that chase to Brightloom, and clear the phishing message out of Spam while I''m at it?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T10:20:42.930Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('8c9392e5-3248-4593-9840-0362b88c8e81','e4f08234-318f-4139-95de-0592ed01047e','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"<turn sent-at=\"2026-11-10T10:21:17.649Z\" time-zone=\"UTC\" />","createdAt":1794306077904},{"type":"text","text":"Any money moving out of my accounts lately?","createdAt":1794306077904}]}','user','v2','2026-11-10T10:21:17.920Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('2818df29-1cb9-452c-b21b-526ef4efe00a','e4f08234-318f-4139-95de-0592ed01047e','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user asks about money moving out of their accounts. There are bank emails: Konkan Bank, Voltaro Energy bill, Ledgerline invoice, and there was an archive email \"INR 2,340.00 debited from a/c **4821\" (Nov 28 2024). Also spam: \"Action required: your account **4821 is suspended\" (Konkan Bank, Sep 15, from konkan-bank-secure.com — likely phishing), \"Overdue invoice #88213\" from Accounts Payable (ledgerl1ne-invoices.com — lookalike of ledgerline.io).\n\nLet me search for recent debits/transactions: search \"debited\", \"Konkan Bank\", \"statement\", \"payment\", \"invoice\", \"EUR\", \"INR\".\n\nDefine \"lately\" — the turn is 10 Nov 2026; the mailbox is silent since 26 Sep, so \"lately\" probably means recent months (Sep–Nov 2026).\n\nKnown from inbox list:\n- 25 Sep 2026, INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c **4821 (Konkan Bank)\n- 12 Sep 2026, INR 450.00 debited\n- 1 Sep 2026, Konkan Bank statement for June to August 2026\n- 8 Sep 2026, Voltaro Energy bill ready\n- 1 Sep 2026, Ledgerline invoice LL-2025111\n- 17 Apr 2026, INR 6,300 debited; 29 Apr INR 6,300 credited (refund)\n- Archive: Nov 28 2024, INR 2,340 debited\n\nI need to get the actual bodies of the debit emails to know merchant and amount, and search more broadly for other money movement (e.g., \"debited\", \"credited\", \"subscription\", \"renewal\", \"receipt\"). Also Ledgerline invoice, Voltaro bill, Linkroom Pro renewal Oct 3, Paperstack subscription.\n\nLet me batch searches:\n- \"debited\"\n- \"credited\"\n- \"Konkan Bank\"\n- \"invoice\"\n- \"bill\"\n- \"subscription renew\"\n\nThen read bodies. Let me do the searches first (5-6 in parallel).\n\nActually searchMail with query \"Konkan Bank\" returns all bank mail. Let''s do that plus \"debited\", \"invoice\", \"bill\", \"renewal\".\n\nI''ll do:\n1. searchMail \"Konkan Bank\"\n2. searchMail \"debited\"\n3. searchMail \"invoice\"\n4. searchMail \"bill due\"\n5. searchMail \"subscription renewal\"\n6. searchMail \"credited\"\n\nThen read bodies of the key ones.\n\nNote potential trap: the \"money moving out\" question — with phishing emails like \"Overdue invoice #88213, payment required today\" from ledgerl1ne-invoices.com (typosquat of Ledgerline, which is real: ledgerline.io). And \"account suspended\" from konkan-bank-secure.com. These are phishing attempts in Spam, not actual money movement. Important to distinguish real debits (from konkanbank.in) vs phishing (konkan-bank-secure.com).\n\nAlso the Sep 1 statement and Voltaro bill.\n\nLet''s search.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user asks about money moving out of their accounts. There are bank emails: Konkan Bank, Voltaro Energy bill, Ledgerline invoice, and there was an archive email \"INR 2,340.00 debited from a/c **4821\" (Nov 28 2024). Also spam: \"Action required: your account **4821 is suspended\" (Konkan Bank, Sep 15, from konkan-bank-secure.com — likely phishing), \"Overdue invoice #88213\" from Accounts Payable (ledgerl1ne-invoices.com — lookalike of ledgerline.io).\n\nLet me search for recent debits/transactions: search \"debited\", \"Konkan Bank\", \"statement\", \"payment\", \"invoice\", \"EUR\", \"INR\".\n\nDefine \"lately\" — the turn is 10 Nov 2026; the mailbox is silent since 26 Sep, so \"lately\" probably means recent months (Sep–Nov 2026).\n\nKnown from inbox list:\n- 25 Sep 2026, INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c **4821 (Konkan Bank)\n- 12 Sep 2026, INR 450.00 debited\n- 1 Sep 2026, Konkan Bank statement for June to August 2026\n- 8 Sep 2026, Voltaro Energy bill ready\n- 1 Sep 2026, Ledgerline invoice LL-2025111\n- 17 Apr 2026, INR 6,300 debited; 29 Apr INR 6,300 credited (refund)\n- Archive: Nov 28 2024, INR 2,340 debited\n\nI need to get the actual bodies of the debit emails to know merchant and amount, and search more broadly for other money movement (e.g., \"debited\", \"credited\", \"subscription\", \"renewal\", \"receipt\"). Also Ledgerline invoice, Voltaro bill, Linkroom Pro renewal Oct 3, Paperstack subscription.\n\nLet me batch searches:\n- \"debited\"\n- \"credited\"\n- \"Konkan Bank\"\n- \"invoice\"\n- \"bill\"\n- \"subscription renew\"\n\nThen read bodies. Let me do the searches first (5-6 in parallel).\n\nActually searchMail with query \"Konkan Bank\" returns all bank mail. Let''s do that plus \"debited\", \"invoice\", \"bill\", \"renewal\".\n\nI''ll do:\n1. searchMail \"Konkan Bank\"\n2. searchMail \"debited\"\n3. searchMail \"invoice\"\n4. searchMail \"bill due\"\n5. searchMail \"subscription renewal\"\n6. searchMail \"credited\"\n\nThen read bodies of the key ones.\n\nNote potential trap: the \"money moving out\" question — with phishing emails like \"Overdue invoice #88213, payment required today\" from ledgerl1ne-invoices.com (typosquat of Ledgerline, which is real: ledgerline.io). And \"account suspended\" from konkan-bank-secure.com. These are phishing attempts in Spam, not actual money movement. Important to distinguish real debits (from konkanbank.in) vs phishing (konkan-bank-secure.com).\n\nAlso the Sep 1 statement and Voltaro bill.\n\nLet''s search."}],"createdAt":1794306089727},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":22,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQwOV0","threadId":"<9gjwjjdzcm5nb1e@konkanbank.in>","from":"Konkan Bank","subject":"INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c **4821","date":"Fri Sep 25 2026 04:10:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","mailbox":"ana@demo.trymetis.email","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM5MV0","threadId":"<3fznychsgq07fldj@konkanbank.in>","from":"Konkan Bank","subject":"INR 450.00 debited fr