ait, page 311 returned Apr 11 ... Jan 12, and token 301. And page 351 returned Jul 22 ... Jan 12 too, token 301. Overlap; tokens seem non-monotonic/opaque. Hmm.\n6. pageToken 301 → Jan 12 2026 → Nov 2024, token 251? Actually page 301 returned Jan 12 2026 back to Jan 12? It returned \"Priya Nair 12 Jan 2026\" as last... no.\n\nLet me re-read: page 301 (the one I called with 301) returned Apr 11 2026 → ... → Jan 12 2026 (Priya Nair \"Type licences for 2026\"), token 301. Hmm, that was the call with pageToken 311? I''m confusing myself.\n\nOrder of my calls:\n- Batch A: pageToken 401 and pageToken 361 (both 50 items).\n- Batch B: pageToken 351 and pageToken 311 (both 50 items).\n- Batch C: pageToken 261 (10 items) and sent/30, archive/80.\n\nWait no. Let me recheck. Batch A was \"pageToken 401\" and \"pageToken 361\"? Looking: I called listEmails(pageToken=401) and listEmails(pageToken=361)? The first batch returned: page 401 → Sep 18 → Jul 22 (token 351); page 361 → Aug 4 → Apr 12 (token 311). Hmm, actually the results I got: first result ended at \"Codeyard #57 Jul 22\" with token 351; second ended at \"Brightloom A-31 Apr 12\" with token 311. And I passed 401 and 361. OK.\n\nThen batch B: I passed 351 and 311. Results: 351 → Jul 22 build failed → Jan 12 (token 301); 311 → Apr 11 → Jan 12 (token 301). Hmm both ended at Jan 12 with token 301, consistent-ish.\n\nThen batch C: I passed 301? No — I passed 261 and 251? Let me check: I called listEmails(folder=inbox, pageToken=261) in one batch with sent 30 and archive 80 — that returned Jan 1 2026 → Jun 2025? Actually result showed Jan 1 2026 ... then Nov 2024 ... no.\n\nHonestly the paging is muddled and the counts overlap, so I can''t derive an exact total this way reliably.\n\nKey insight though: **in the inbox, essentially every email I have seen is `isRead: true`.** The unread ones (`isRead: false`) appeared only in Spam and in the Edge Sender batch (inbox edge messages from Jun 10 2024, if those are in the inbox... 