one thing — a 200-message synthetic \"Re: Long thread\" thread plus ~78 other Edge Sender test fixtures; none of it is actual correspondence. Every real message (132 of them) is read.\n\nLet me verify the composition of the 278:\n- 200 messages: \"Re: Long thread\" (indices 51..250) = 200 items (indices 51-250 inclusive = 200).\n- att-* : indices 251..268 = 18 items (att-zero-byte 251 ... att-mislabeled-zip-as-pdf 268).\n- jsonld-*: 269..274 = 6.\n- html-*: 275..278 = 4.\n- 1..50: misc edge (date, enc, img, max, mime, min, thread loops...).\nTotal: 200 + 18 + 6 + 4 + 50 = 278. ✓ \n\nSo 278 unread = 200-message thread + 78 other fixtures.\n\nGreat, consistent. Answer with the mailbox name and the caveat that the count is from paging the folder (410 messages, 278 unread, 132 read), and that unread is entirely fixtures — no real mail is unread. Also offer to mark them read or delete.\n\nWait, one more check: are the \"att-ics-*\" indices 251..260? att-zero-byte 251... att-ics-rrule-secondly 260 → 260..251 = 10 items: zero-byte(251), no-filename(252), hostile-filenames(253), binary-30mb(254), pdf-empty(255), pdf-corrupt(256), pdf-2000-pages(257), ics-invalid(258), ics-10000-events(259), ics-rrule-secondly(260). So att-* total = 251..268 = 18. ✓\n\nAnd indices 1..50 list: 42,44,38,50,49,48,47,46,37,36,35,34,33,32,31,30,29,28,27,26,25,24,23,22,21,20,19,18,17,16,15,14,13,12,11,10,9,8,7,6,5,4,45,43,40,39,3,2,1 = 48? Let me count: 42,44,38 (3), 50,49,48,47,46 (5→8), 37,36,35,34,33,32,31,30,29,28,27,26,25,24,23,22,21,20,19,18,17,16,15,14,13,12,11,10,9,8,7,6,5,4 (34→42), 45,43,40,39 (4→46), 3,2,1 (3→49). Hmm 49? Missing 41 = \"date-epoch\" which appeared in the same page. Yes 41 was there. So 50. ✓ Good.\n\nSo the answer: 278 unread.\n\nAlso note: 0 unread in the sense of \"real\" mail. And the read-later list is empty, snoozed empty.\n\nI''ll answer concisely with the breakdown and offer cleanup."}],"createdAt":1794306287787},{"type":"text","text":"**278 unread — but not one 