nth. Wait: results were Sep 7 (Codeyard), Sep 2 (Paperstack), Aug 24 (Codeyard), Jul 27 (Codeyard), Jul 2 (Paperstack), Jun 29 (Codeyard), Jun 1 (Codeyard), May 2 (Paperstack), Mar 2 (Paperstack), Jan 2 (Paperstack), Nov 2 2025 (Paperstack) = 11. So 5 Codeyard digests, 6 Paperstack months.\n\n3. **Paperstack** — \"Your Paperstack month: <Month> <Year>\" monthly recap: Sep 2026, Jul 2026, May 2026, Mar 2026, Jan 2026, Nov 2025 = 6 visible. (Feb/Apr/Jun/Aug/Oct seem absent — interesting gap, maybe not sent.)\n\n4. **Priya Nair — [Fernhill Team] Studio weekly** — internal weekly digest of their studio: Sep 14 2026, Jul 13 2026, May 11 2026, Feb 9 2026, Nov 10 2025, Sep 15 2025, Jul 14 2025, May 12 2025, Mar 10 2025, Jan 13 2025 = 10. This is an internal digest — the user''s own team. Worth flagging as \"yours, not a subscription\".\n\n5. **Linkroom** — product update broadcasts: \"Linkroom for teams: shared recordings\" (Sep 8 2026), \"Breakout rooms are here\" (Apr 21 2026), \"Linkroom rooms now remember your layout\" (Sep 23 2025), \"New in Linkroom: live captions in 12 languages\" (Feb 18 2025). These are product marketing, 4 items.\n\n6. **Northbeam Air** — marketing/broadcast: \"Fly to Osaka from Frankfurt, new route from October\" (Jun 16 2026), \"Summer in Lisbon: city breaks from EUR 79\" (Jun 10 2025), \"Fares to Tokyo from EUR 689 return\" (Jan 22 2025, trash), \"Your miles are about to expire\" (Feb 3 2026, trash) — marketing, mostly promo.\n\n7. **Tavola** — \"Where Lisbon eats on Sundays\" (Mar 6 2026, archive), \"Autumn menus worth booking\" (Oct 3 2025, archive), and an unsubscribe confirmation \"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks\" (Mar 7 2026). So Tavola newsletter was already unsubscribed. That''s a good detail.\n\n8. Spam has marketing junk: \"SEO Growth Team – Get Fernhill Studio to page one of Google\", \"Instagram Growth – 10,000 real followers\", \"Business Funding – pre-approved EUR 50,000\", \"Lottery Department\", \"Global Design Summit invitation\", \"Domain renewal notice\". Those are promotional spam — cold outreach, not newsletters you subscribed to. Maybe mention separately as cold pitches in Spam.\n\nVoltaro Energy \"bill is ready\" — transactional, not newsletter. Konkan statements — transactional.\n\nAlso the trash contains older Kestrel newsletters (deleted by the user earlier) — many.\n\nNow the ask: \"Find emails that look like newsletters or digests.\" Present as list grouped by sender with counts, dates range, where they live (inbox vs archive vs trash), and note the label `newsletter` exists. Then offer to label/archive.\n\nNote: a good insight — the \"This week at Kestrel\" is by far the biggest: 56 weekly issues + 5 promos = 61 Kestrel broadcasts; ~all from a shop you''ve never bought from (no Kestrel order in the mail). And Tavola is unsubscribed already.\n\nLet me structure the answer:\n\nHeadline: ~85 newsletter/digest emails in ana@demo.trymetis.email, from 8 senders.\n\nTable: Sender | Pattern | Cadence | Count | Range | Where.\n\nThen notes: internal vs external, the promo broadcasts, the spam cold pitches, Tavola unsubscribed.\n\nCounts:\n- Kestrel: 56 \"This week at...\" + 5 one-off promos = 61\n- Codeyard digest: 5\n- Paperstack month: 6\n- Fernhill Studio weekly (your own team, Priya): 10\n- Linkroom product updates: 4\n- Northbeam Air marketing: 4 (2 in trash/archive)\n- Tavola: 2 + unsubscribe confirmation\n- Spam cold pitches: 6\n\nTotal editorial/marketing ≈ 61+5+6+4+4+2 = 82. I''ll say \"about 80\".\n\nCareful with the Fernhill studio weekly count: I saw Sep 14 2026, Jul 13 2026, May 11 2026, Feb 9 2026 (4 in 2026), Nov 10 2025, Sep 15 2025, Jul 14 2025, May 12 2025, Mar 10 2025, Jan 13 2025 (6 in 2025) = 10.\n\nCodeyard digests: Sep 7, Aug 24, Jul 27, Jun 29, Jun 1 2026 = 5. Also possibly earlier ones exist but weren''t matched (query \"digest\"). Fine — say \"at least 5 on record\".\n\nLinkroom: Sep 8 2026, Apr 21 2026, Sep 23 2025, Feb 18 2025 = 4.\n\nNorthbeam: Jun 16 2026 (archive), Jun 10 2025 (archive), Jan 22 2025 (trash), Feb 3 2026 (trash).\n\nTavola: archive Mar 6 2026, Oct 3 2025, plus Mar 7 2026 unsubscribe note.\n\nSpam: SEO Growth Team (Mar 18 2026), Instagram Growth (Oct 21 2025), Business Funding (Jan 29 2026), Lottery (Aug 14 2025), Global Design Summit (Dec 8 2025), Domain Services (Jun 11 2026), Mail Administrator mailbox full (Aug 19 2026), Codeyard \"account will be deleted\" (Sep 2 2026) — that last is phishing too.\n\nI''ll keep spam as a short separate note.\n\nOffer: label them `newsletter` / `promotional`, or bulk archive; suggest unsubscribing Kestrel.\n\nWrite it up scannably."}],"createdAt":1794306342704},{"type":"text","text":"**About 80, from 7 real senders — and one of them is 61 of them.** All in **ana@demo.trymetis.email**.\n\n## The bulk: retail newsletter\n| Sender | Pattern | Cadence | Count | Span |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kestrel Supply Co.** | *This week at Kestrel: <theme>* | weekly | **56** | Nov 2024 → 26 Sep 2026 |\n| Kestrel Supply Co. | one-off promos (*15% off this weekend only*, *Spring sale starts now*, 2× Black Friday, Mother''s Day) | — | 5 | Nov 2024 → Aug 2026 |\n\nThe themes rotate through just four variants — *A kitchen for slow mornings*, *The candle edit*, *Stoneware from Porto*, *Gifts under EUR 30* — plus *Meet the maker: Oficina Lume* and a kintsugi workshop. It''s the single biggest sender in your mailbox, it arrives every week like clockwork, and **you have never bought anything from Kestrel** — there''s no order, receipt or shipping mail from them anywhere. Older issues are already being deleted by hand: several sit in Trash.\n\n## Product digests\n| Sender | Pattern | Count | Latest |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Codeyard** | *Your weekly Codeyard digest* | 5 on record | 7 Sep 2026 |\n| **Paperstack** | *Your Paperstack month: <Month>* — monthly recap | 6 | Sep 2026 |\n| **Linkroom** | product announcements (*Breakout rooms are here*, *live captions in 12 languages*, *shared recordings*) | 4 | 8 Sep 2026 |\n| **Northbeam Air** | fare and route marketing (*city breaks from EUR 79*, *Fly to Osaka*) | 4 | Jun 2026 |\n\nNote the Codeyard digest is quiet since 7 Sep and the Paperstack recap skips months — Feb, Apr, Jun and Aug 2026 have no \"month\" mail, so it''s been inconsistent rather than stopped.\n\n## Internal — not a subscription\n**Priya Nair — *[Fernhill Team] Studio weekly*** — **10 issues**, Jan 2025 → 14 Sep 2026. Same digest shape as the newsletters, but it''s your own studio''s roundup, so it belongs in `work`, not `newsletter`.\n\n## Already dealt with\n**Tavola** — *Where Lisbon eats on Sundays* and *Autumn menus worth booking*, then on 7 Mar 2026: **\"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks.\"** Gone. That''s the one you''ve already shut off.\n\n## Not newsletters, but pretending to be mail you want\nSix cold pitches sat in **Spam** — *Get Fernhill Studio to page one of Google*, *10,000 real followers for your studio*, *Pre-approved: EUR 50,000*, *you have won EUR 850,000*, a *Global Design Summit* speaking invite and a domain-renewal notice. Cold outreach, not lists you joined.\n\nTwo cleanups I''d suggest: **label the Kestrel block `newsletter`** so it stops mixing with real mail, and **unsubscribe from Kestrel** — 56 issues and no purchase means it''s pure noise. Want me to do either, or sweep all ~80 out of the inbox into Archive?","createdAt":1794306342704}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**About 80, from 7 real senders — and one of them is 61 of them.** All in **ana@demo.trymetis.email**.\n\n## The bulk: retail newsletter\n| Sender | Pattern | Cadence | Count | Span |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kestrel Supply Co.** | *This week at Kestrel: <theme>* | weekly | **56** | Nov 2024 → 26 Sep 2026 |\n| Kestrel Supply Co. | one-off promos (*15% off this weekend only*, *Spring sale starts now*, 2× Black Friday, Mother''s Day) | — | 5 | Nov 2024 → Aug 2026 |\n\nThe themes rotate through just four variants — *A kitchen for slow mornings*, *The candle edit*, *Stoneware from Porto*, *Gifts under EUR 30* — plus *Meet the maker: Oficina Lume* and a kintsugi workshop. It''s the single biggest sender in your mailbox, it arrives every week like clockwork, and **you have never bought anything from Kestrel** — there''s no order, receipt or shipping mail from them anywhere. Older issues are already being deleted by hand: several sit in Trash.\n\n## Product digests\n| Sender | Pattern | Count | Latest |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Codeyard** | *Your weekly Codeyard digest* | 5 on record | 7 Sep 2026 |\n| **Paperstack** | *Your Paperstack month: <Month>* — monthly recap | 6 | Sep 2026 |\n| **Linkroom** | product announcements (*Breakout rooms are here*, *live captions in 12 languages*, *shared recordings*) | 4 | 8 Sep 2026 |\n| **Northbeam Air** | fare and route marketing (*city breaks from EUR 79*, *Fly to Osaka*) | 4 | Jun 2026 |\n\nNote the Codeyard digest is quiet since 7 Sep and the Paperstack recap skips months — Feb, Apr, Jun and Aug 2026 have no \"month\" mail, so it''s been inconsistent rather than stopped.\n\n## Internal — not a subscription\n**Priya Nair — *[Fernhill Team] Studio weekly*** — **10 issues**, Jan 2025 → 14 Sep 2026. Same digest shape as the newsletters, but it''s your own studio''s roundup, so it belongs in `work`, not `newsletter`.\n\n## Already dealt with\n**Tavola** — *Where Lisbon eats on Sundays* and *Autumn menus worth booking*, then on 7 Mar 2026: **\"You''re unsubscribed from Tavola picks.\"** Gone. That''s the one you''ve already shut off.\n\n## Not newsletters, but pretending to be mail you want\nSix cold pitches sat in **Spam** — *Get Fernhill Studio to page one of Google*, *10,000 real followers for your studio*, *Pre-approved: EUR 50,000*, *you have won EUR 850,000*, a *Global Design Summit* speaking invite and a domain-renewal notice. Cold outreach, not lists you joined.\n\nTwo cleanups I''d suggest: **label the Kestrel block `newsletter`** so it stops mixing with real mail, and **unsubscribe from Kestrel** — 56 issues and no purchase means it''s pure noise. Want me to do either, or sweep all ~80 out of the inbox into Archive?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T10:24:57.033Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
