s an \"edge\" folder in the two S3 buckets, and drive 3 exposes only Clients.\n\nTo answer \"do they have the same files in them?\" — top-level shape is the same, but I need to check contents down a level to see if files match. Let me descend into Clients/ on a few drives and compare, plus the two S3 buckets'' edge folders. That''s a lot of calls but valuable. Let''s do: for each of the 7 drives, list Clients/ (the common folder). 7 calls. Plus edge/ on the two S3s (2 calls). 9 calls in parallel.\n\nActually to compare meaningfully, listing Clients/ across all is the best single test. Let''s do all 7 Clients + 2 edge = 9.\n\nAlso maybe read welcome.txt to see if identical — it''s 182 bytes in all. But reading requires a tool \"read file text\" — need to search for it. Not necessary; the name/size match is enough to say \"same name and size\". Actually size 182 in all 7 → identical size, likely identical file. I''ll note that the sizes match but I haven''t read them.\n\nLet me do the folder listings.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Top levels:\n\n- Drive 1 (sftp, 36600459): Team/, Finance/, Clients/, welcome.txt\n- Drive 2 (ftp, d4dacf11): Clients/, Finance/, Team/, welcome.txt\n- Drive 3 (ftp, 766b212a — scoped): only Clients/\n- Drive 4 (ftp, 42ffd478): Clients/, Finance/, Team/, welcome.txt\n- Drive 5 (webdav, cc3fbded): Team/, Finance/, Clients/, welcome.txt\n- Drive 6 (s3, b4199497): Clients/, Finance/, Team/, edge/, welcome.txt (welcome.txt has null mimeType)\n- Drive 7 (s3, 1ae0b7b1): Clients/, Finance/, Team/, edge/, welcome.txt (null mimeType)\n\nSo the shapes are near-identical: three shared folders (Clients, Finance, Team) in five/six of them, plus an \"edge\" folder in the two S3 buckets, and drive 3 exposes only Clients.\n\nTo answer \"do they have the same files in them?\" — top-level shape is the same, but I need to check contents down a level to see if files match. Let me descend into Clients/ on a few drives and compare, plus the two S3 buckets'' 