oor"},{"type":"text","text":"**One person — you.**\n\n| Name | Email | Role | memberId |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ana Silva | ana@demo.trymetis.email | **owner** | `f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615` |\n\nNo pending invitations either — the invite list is empty, so nobody is waiting to join.\n\nThat single membership explains several things you''ve been looking at:\n\n- **The \"Team\" folder is aspirational.** `Team/` holds a `website/`, an `Offsite 2026/`, the Aozora logo PNG, a voice memo and a meeting note — but there is no teammate in this workspace to share them with. The note''s attendees (Raj, Tomás, Kenji) are people in your mail, not members here.\n- **\"Ask Sam for access to Finance/\"** in `welcome.txt` — Sam isn''t a workspace member, so that instruction can''t be completed from inside this workspace.\n- **The mirrors are for your benefit only.** Seven drives holding the same corpus makes sense when one person is syncing several endpoints; it isn''t a shared-team setup.\n- **Anything scoped to a colleague can''t resolve.** I can still answer questions about Raj Mehta or Priya Nair from your mail and calendars — `findMemberMail` and `findMemberEvents` key off address-book and calendar data — but they aren''t workspace members, so their connected drives won''t appear.\n\nYou''re also the owner, which means the workspace-level tools are yours: inviting people, creating and toggling workflows, and managing those seven drive connections. Want me to invite someone, or look at what Raj or Priya has on their calendar?","createdAt":1794306452348}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**One person — you.**\n\n| Name | Email | Role | memberId |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ana Silva | ana@demo.trymetis.email | **owner** | `f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615` |\n\nNo pending invitations either — the invite list is empty, so nobody is waiting to join.\n\nThat single membership explains several things you''ve been looking at:\n\n- **The \"Team\" folder is aspirational.** `Team/` holds a `website/`, an `Offsite 2026/`, the Aozora logo PNG, a voice memo and a meeting note — but there is no teammate in this workspace to share them with. The note''s attendees (Raj, Tomás, Kenji) are people in your mail, not members here.\n- **\"Ask Sam for access to Finance/\"** in `welcome.txt` — Sam isn''t a workspace member, so that instruction can''t be completed from inside this workspace.\n- **The mirrors are for your benefit only.** Seven drives holding the same corpus makes sense when one person is syncing several endpoints; it isn''t a shared-team setup.\n- **Anything scoped to a colleague can''t resolve.** I can still answer questions about Raj Mehta or Priya Nair from your mail and calendars — `findMemberMail` and `findMemberEvents` key off address-book and calendar data — but they aren''t workspace members, so their connected drives won''t appear.\n\nYou''re also the owner, which means the workspace-level tools are yours: inviting people, creating and toggling workflows, and managing those seven drive connections. Want me to invite someone, or look at what Raj or Priya has on their calendar?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-10T10:27:20.088Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
