INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('24bc421c-f115-4925-bda3-950a58d3f6f4','e4f08234-318f-4139-95de-0592ed01047e','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user wants a prioritized to-do list for this week based on everything above. \"This week\" — turn sent-at 2026-11-10T10:23 UTC (Monday, Nov 10, 2026 — let me check: Nov 10 2026 is a Tuesday? Let''s compute: Jan 1 2026 is Thursday. Nov 10 2026... Let''s compute day of week. 2026-11-10. Known: 2026-09-26 is a Saturday per the email dates (\"Sat Sep 26 2026\"). So Sep 26 Sat → Oct 3 Sat, Oct 10 Sat, Oct 17, Oct 24, Oct 31, Nov 7 Sat → Nov 9 Mon, Nov 10 Tue. So Nov 10 2026 is a Tuesday. Week: Mon Nov 9 – Sun Nov 15, 2026.\n\nI need to gather state for this week: calendar events, mail needing replies, drafts, scheduled, snoozed, workflow runs maybe. I have knowledge from earlier turns? Actually this conversation''s earlier turns were about the inbox (278 unread fixtures), newsletters, drives, members. But my actual knowledge of the mailbox contents came from earlier turns'' tool results in this conversation — the inbox listing showed emails from Sep/Oct/Nov 2026. I have a fair amount of context: deadlines? Let me recall notable items from the inbox pages I fetched:\n\nThings I saw in the inbox (real mail, indices 279–410, dates Nov 2024 → Sep 26 2026). Wait — the newest inbox item is Sep 26 2026 (Kestrel \"This week at the shop\"), index 410. So \"now\" is Nov 10 2026 and the inbox''s newest is Sep 26 2026? That''s odd — the turn clock says Nov 10, 2026, and the mailbox''s latest mail is Sep 26. Hmm, so there''s a gap of 6 weeks with no mail? Possibly the fixtures. Anyway.\n\nI recall these real items from listings (from the pages I fetched earlier):\n- Sep 25/26 2026: Kestrel newsletter (Sep 26). \n- \"Re: Aozora rebrand: brief and timeline\" from Kenji Watanabe (Aug 11) and Priya? \n- \"Fernhill Studio — September invoicing\" from