bon\"\n- Voltaro Energy bill, Konkan Bank statements\n- Codeyard, Paperstack digests\n\nBut I don''t have precise recall of the many subjects. To build a credible prioritized to-do list, I should gather fresh data: \n1. Calendar events for this week (need listEvents tool — search for it).\n2. Mail needing attention — recent inbox, unread/starred, drafts, scheduled, snoozed. aggregateInbox could give recent per mailbox (though the newest mail is Sep 2026... aggregateInbox gives most recent, which will be Sep 2026 items).\n3. Maybe workflow runs? Probably not necessary.\n\nAlso there were promises in the earlier turns'' analysis: e.g., the newsletter cleanup, the drive mirror issue, the internal digest. Plus an unresolved thing: \"Ask Sam for access to Finance/\".\n\nLet me search for tools: \"calendar events list this week\", \"create calendar event\", \"draft email\", \"send email\", \"labels\", \"workflows\". I need listEvents mainly. Let me search: \"list calendar events window\" and \"create draft email\" and \"labels list apply\".\n\nThen call: listEvents for Nov 9–15, aggregateInbox, listEmails starred, listEmails drafts, listScheduled, listSnoozed, listCalendars.\n\nThat''s a lot but let''s batch: first search tools (calendar events, drafts/send, labels, workflows).\n\nActually to keep it efficient: do the tool searches now, then next turn do the data gathering in one big batch.\n\nSearch queries:\n1. \"calendar events list window create event\"\n2. \"draft email send message reply\"\n3. \"labels list apply label\"\n4. \"scheduled emails snoozed read later\" — I already have listSnoozed/listScheduled.\n5. \"workflow runs\" — maybe skip.\n\nLet me do 3 searches in parallel."}],"createdAt":1794306467122},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"findMemberEvents","description":"List calendar events in a time window that one workspace member organises or is invited to, across every visible calendar in the workspace