ailbox.","score":7.17}],"loaded":["createDraft","sendEmail","retryScheduled","getRawEmail","deleteDraft"],"message":"Found and loaded 5 tool(s): createDraft, sendEmail, retryScheduled, getRawEmail, deleteDraft. They are available on your next turn — call them directly."},"toolCallId":"call_2e83394591a341bbb2b80015","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"create draft reply send email message"}},"updatedAt":1794306467127},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"listLabels","description":"List every label key available in this workspace: the built-in labels plus custom labels. Use these exact keys with setLabel.","score":16.62},{"name":"deleteLabel","description":"Delete a custom label from a specific mailbox. Built-in labels cannot be deleted.","score":10.72},{"name":"setLabels","description":"Set the same label on several emails in a specific mailbox at once. The label must be an existing key from listLabels. Returns each email''s previou...","score":8.66},{"name":"starEmail","description":"Star or unstar an email in a specific mailbox.","score":8.18},{"name":"archiveEmail","description":"Archive an email in a specific mailbox — it leaves the inbox but is not deleted.","score":7.57}],"loaded":["listLabels","deleteLabel","setLabels","starEmail","archiveEmail"],"message":"Found and loaded 5 tool(s): listLabels, deleteLabel, setLabels, starEmail, archiveEmail. They are available on your next turn — call them directly. Some were already loaded."},"toolCallId":"call_25ac04970e074c2b8860bb6b","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"labels list apply label archive star message"}},"updatedAt":1794306467127},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1794306467130,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now gather data. Batch:\n1. listCalendars (need calendar ids? listEvents can go across every visible calendar without ids — fine, but listing calendars is useful to name calendars. listEvents returns accountEmail and calendarName per result, so maybe skip listCalendars.)\n2. listEvents timeMin 2026-11-09T00:00:00Z, timeMax 2026-11-16T00:00:00Z (Mon–Sun). Maybe extend to Nov 22 to catch \"next week\" items? Keep to this week: Nov 9 00:00 → Nov 16 00:00.\n3. aggregateInbox perMailbox 25 (only one mailbox? There''s just ana@demo.trymetis.email? Earlier I only ever saw one mailbox. Let me call listMailboxes to be safe — it''s always loaded and cheap. Hmm, I did use a specific mailboxId from earlier turns consistently. But are there other mailboxes? The workspace might have more. Earlier in the conversation, my inbox listings were of that one mailbox; I never called listMailboxes in this conversation (I may have in a prior turn not shown). The system says call listMailboxes when you need a mailboxId you cannot name. I have the id. But for \"everything above\" a workspace-wide view would be good. Let me include listMailboxes to be safe — cheap.\n4. listEmails starred (folder=starred, limit 25) \n5. listEmails drafts (folder=drafts)\n6. listSnoozed, listScheduled\n7. listLabels (for the newsletter label offer)\n8. listPins (folders pinned — maybe useful for drive task context) — optional, skip? Could be nice. Include.\n\nThat''s 8 calls. Fine, batch them.\n\nWait: listEmails requires mailboxId and folder. Use 2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134. But if there are other mailboxes, I''d want them too. Let me first do listMailboxes... but batching means I can''t use the result. I''ll batch everything with the known mailbox and also call listMailboxes; if there are more mailboxes, I can follow up.\n\nLet''s go.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now gather data. Batch:\n1. listCalendars (need calendar ids? listEvents can go across every visible calendar without ids — fine, but listing calendars is useful to name calendars. listEvents returns accountEmail and calendarName per result, so maybe skip listCalendars.)\n2. listEvents timeMin 2026-