v 9–15).** The user asks for a prioritized to-do list \"based on everything above\" — i.e., combining mail, calendars, drives, members, and this week''s constraints. I should produce a prioritized list with concrete actions, each with the tool I''d use, and offer to execute.\n\nNote the \"now\" nuance: it''s Tue Nov 10, 10:27 UTC. The 1:1 with Raj was 10:00–10:30 UTC → in progress, ends in ~3 min. Flag gently.\n\nAlso the timezone trap: Tokyo trip means she''s in JST (UTC+9). Daily standup at 09:00 UTC = 18:00 JST — so the standup runs at dinner time in Tokyo. The 1:1 at 10:00 UTC = 19:00 JST.\n\nPrioritization:\n\n**P0 — time-bound today/this week**\n1. Weekly 1:1 Ana/Raj — right now, ends 10:30 UTC (19:00 JST). If it''s on, go.\n2. Tokyo trip Nov 9–15 — you''re in Tokyo all week; the flight is Northbeam NB7Q4K (Lisbon→Tokyo Nov 9). Check the Sep 17 schedule change. Nothing else is on the calendar this week except standups at 18:00 JST and 85 \"Bulk NNN\" placeholder events that are noise.\n3. Scheduled mail \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" is parked at 2099-01-05 — it will never send. Fix or delete. (This is the only scheduled item; and it''s to yourself.)\n\n**P1 — client work with a real person waiting**\n4. Layla Haddad (Saffron & Sage) — Arabic menu design thread (Jul 8) + your unsent draft reply sitting since Sep 18. Two months of silence on a client deliverable.\n5. Kenji Watanabe (Aozora) — 新ブランド案のご確認について (Sep 10) has no reply in the mailbox; plus the packaging call was Oct 15. And his brief/timeline is starred.\n6. Priya''s \"Arabic proofs\" (Sep 18) — likely the input to the Layla reply; nothing sent.\n7. Lena Hoffmann / Kaltwasser — \"AW: Rechnung FS-2026-031\" (Jul 21, starred, German) — invoice FS-2026-031 unanswered for ~4 months.\n8. Mira Costa — Aozora launch venue thread, your only recent star (Sep 9) — unresolved.\n9. Raj: Rebrand kickoff (Sep 21) + Aozora review agenda — check nothing was left hanging after the Oct 8 review.\n\n**P2 — housekeeping t